WEBVTT

00:36.040 --> 00:44.810
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:44.850 --> 00:53.850
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

00:53.890 --> 01:00.620
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:03.230 --> 01:09.300
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:11.470 --> 01:20.040
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:20.080 --> 01:26.680
And I'm faced with another day

01:27.890 --> 01:33.620
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:33.660 --> 01:37.960
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:38.000 --> 01:42.440
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:42.470 --> 01:46.870
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:46.910 --> 01:51.400
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:51.450 --> 01:59.290
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:20.060 --> 02:24.230
Geez, I can't even tell left from right.

02:25.270 --> 02:27.400
Don't you think we should head back?

02:33.820 --> 02:36.070
Geez, what are they thinking?

02:36.160 --> 02:38.660
Is it really in a place like this?

02:38.990 --> 02:42.790
Rumors I hear with these
long ears of mine are never wrong.

02:43.120 --> 02:45.450
I think it should be somewhere around here.

02:48.670 --> 02:51.080
Come on, let's go back!

02:52.420 --> 02:56.720
How annoying... If you want
to go back, go back on your own.

02:56.920 --> 02:58.220
B-O-Y.

03:01.350 --> 03:02.550
This scent...

03:02.680 --> 03:03.890
It's this way.

03:15.400 --> 03:16.570
Here it is.

03:22.160 --> 03:23.240
That's strange.

03:23.950 --> 03:25.320
Mataichi-san!

03:25.530 --> 03:26.830
Ogin-san!

03:31.710 --> 03:32.290
This is...

03:32.370 --> 03:33.330
<i>yummy!</i>

03:33.420 --> 03:35.120
It has the same flavor as the ones Kyougokutei makes!

03:35.130 --> 03:36.580
I'm moved to tears!

03:37.840 --> 03:40.000
Is it good? Is it?

03:41.460 --> 03:45.800
[Note: Shiratama (rice flour dumplings) and kuromame (black beans)
are common ingredients in traditional Japanese desserts.]

03:41.460 --> 03:43.510
I'm this inn's attraction, Shiratama.

03:43.840 --> 03:45.800
I'm the other attraction, Kuromame.

03:45.840 --> 03:47.720
Shiratama and Kuromame?

03:47.800 --> 03:48.970
Have we met somewhere?

03:49.640 --> 03:50.510
You guys!

03:55.440 --> 03:56.850
White Hag...

03:56.890 --> 03:58.270
and Black Hag!

03:58.980 --> 04:00.360
You fooled us.

04:00.690 --> 04:03.190
We have a small favor to ask of you, see?

04:03.280 --> 04:06.070
And now that you've eaten, you're
obligated to help us, see?

04:08.150 --> 04:10.240
But before that, about that kid...

04:10.410 --> 04:11.700
Yes, about that kid...

04:37.720 --> 04:38.760
Help m--

04:45.480 --> 04:46.350
How is he?

04:46.480 --> 04:49.570
Well, I'd be surprised if he survived the night.

04:50.650 --> 04:53.530
Give him something to eat that will bolster his strength.

04:53.530 --> 04:55.950
If you do, he may live.

05:55.210 --> 05:56.330
What did you say?

05:56.920 --> 06:00.590
Then you don't remember anything
that's happened over the last few days?

06:00.880 --> 06:01.670
No, I don't.

06:03.130 --> 06:08.010
I had retired from Ikomaya at Kyoubashi,
and was thinking up children's riddles.

06:08.680 --> 06:13.390
And I was thinking that I'd like to
collect kaidan and write 100 Stories...

06:13.600 --> 06:15.850
Ah, kaidan?

06:17.370 --> 06:19.350
Momosuke

06:17.370 --> 06:19.350
Yamaoka

06:19.610 --> 06:22.770
Are you Momosuke Yamaoka?

06:23.570 --> 06:25.320
It appears that you saved me.

06:25.490 --> 06:26.900
Thank you.

06:26.900 --> 06:28.570
I'll be fine now.

06:32.910 --> 06:34.950
Please don't overexert yourself.

06:37.790 --> 06:42.380
You may have experienced something terrifying.

06:44.090 --> 06:49.380
They say that when people experience such
things, they forget about them sometimes.

07:13.740 --> 07:14.860
What's wrong?

07:15.410 --> 07:17.070
A-A horse!

07:19.580 --> 07:21.330
Look closely.

07:28.250 --> 07:31.210
This was one of my master's favorite horses, Hayate.

07:31.590 --> 07:36.170
Now that you mention it, I want
to thank your master for taking care of me...

07:37.470 --> 07:39.010
Is something wrong?

07:39.050 --> 07:40.720
Well, umm...

07:40.720 --> 07:43.470
The master is away right now.

07:44.680 --> 07:46.810
Then perhaps his wife?

07:46.810 --> 07:49.230
His wife has passed away.

08:38.480 --> 08:40.270
Is anyone here?

08:41.440 --> 08:43.030
M-My stomach...

08:46.820 --> 08:47.900
What's wrong?

08:50.120 --> 08:52.030
M-My stomach suddenly...

08:54.580 --> 08:55.700
I'll call the clerk!

08:55.910 --> 08:59.960
A horse... There's a horse... a black horse...

09:00.040 --> 09:01.790
Horses can't get inside the house.

09:02.330 --> 09:04.920
Oh no! Hayate's picture has...

09:05.050 --> 09:05.710
What?

09:13.090 --> 09:15.640
What are you doing, raising a
racket in the middle of the night?!

09:16.060 --> 09:17.010
Hayate has...

09:19.310 --> 09:20.980
Wh-What is the meaning of this?

09:21.140 --> 09:23.730
I-It's Hayate's ghost.

09:23.850 --> 09:25.900
Don't say foolish things like that!

09:43.910 --> 09:46.580
Huh? My stomach feels better.

09:46.580 --> 09:47.750
Wh-What the...?

09:50.960 --> 09:54.300
Did the horse in that picture sneak out?

09:57.470 --> 10:03.350
The day I was brought here... What did I eat that night?

10:04.020 --> 10:05.180
W-Well...

10:05.270 --> 10:06.470
Please, tell me.

10:08.060 --> 10:09.980
It was horse meat.

10:10.850 --> 10:13.610
H-Horse as in the animal?

10:14.150 --> 10:19.690
We had to. The doctor said
to give you something nourishing.

10:20.070 --> 10:22.360
You killed a horse for me?

10:22.360 --> 10:25.780
No, coincidentally, there was a horse that had just died.

10:29.250 --> 10:30.540
Is something wrong?

10:30.910 --> 10:37.250
[Note: "Shio no Chouji" literally means "Chouji of Salt".]

10:30.910 --> 10:34.540
There's a story called "Shio no Chouji".

10:34.540 --> 10:37.250
There was once a horse breeder named Chouji.

10:37.420 --> 10:43.380
Whenever one of his horses died, he would
eat their flesh after seasoning it with salt and miso.

10:43.380 --> 10:48.550
It's said that one night, the spirit of a
horse appeared, entered Chouji through his mouth,

10:48.560 --> 10:50.720
and raged about within his stomach.

10:52.680 --> 10:54.980
This continued for a hundred days...

10:55.640 --> 11:01.230
According to that Momosuke person, the
stomachache may be caused by a horse's curse.

11:01.360 --> 11:03.440
A horse's curse, you say?

11:05.070 --> 11:07.570
Doctor! You were visiting?

11:07.660 --> 11:11.660
Horses sneaking out of paintings...
Horses cursing humans...

11:11.660 --> 11:13.700
Hah. Merely superstition, I tell you.

11:13.830 --> 11:15.200
B-But...

11:15.620 --> 11:18.460
But more importantly... my medicines.

11:18.670 --> 11:20.210
He needs to drink those.

11:22.290 --> 11:23.630
Understand?

11:23.710 --> 11:26.550
He must drink those before going to bed.

11:27.420 --> 11:28.170
Understood.

11:30.930 --> 11:32.220
Master...

11:33.390 --> 11:36.100
Meat! I want to eat meat!

11:36.600 --> 11:38.930
But if you eat any more...

11:39.350 --> 11:41.350
That meat I ate...

11:41.560 --> 11:43.390
I want to eat that meat.

11:44.650 --> 11:45.610
The meat of a monkey!

11:45.860 --> 11:49.020
Bring that to me this time!

11:58.580 --> 11:59.830
Oh my goodness!

11:59.910 --> 12:01.660
What's the racket about?

12:01.990 --> 12:04.160
Th-The master's daughter has come back...

12:04.750 --> 12:07.040
She's calling herself Osan.

12:07.080 --> 12:08.880
What? The master's daughter?!

12:09.460 --> 12:10.500
Where is she?

12:10.500 --> 12:11.290
In the guest room.

12:26.390 --> 12:27.600
What will we do?

12:44.870 --> 12:48.910
Again... Hayate's ghost is running wild again...

13:11.430 --> 13:14.600
It hurts... My stomach hurts!

13:17.980 --> 13:19.310
Please don't!

13:21.070 --> 13:25.570
If you burn that, Hayate will
rage forever inside your stomach!

13:26.740 --> 13:27.780
Master!

13:28.360 --> 13:31.410
Master? He wasn't away?

13:40.670 --> 13:41.250
It's coming!

13:42.670 --> 13:44.630
Th-That can't be...

13:51.380 --> 13:53.180
S-Save me!

13:53.220 --> 13:54.430
Master!

13:56.560 --> 13:58.260
Save me!

14:05.230 --> 14:07.690
You ate the horse's meat, too, didn't you?

14:07.980 --> 14:09.360
G-Give me medicine.

14:10.030 --> 14:11.480
Medicine won't work.

14:11.780 --> 14:14.450
This is the curse of Shio no Chouji.

14:14.660 --> 14:16.490
Is there nothing we can do?

14:18.160 --> 14:20.490
Save me!

14:22.200 --> 14:24.830
What happened? Please, tell me.

14:25.830 --> 14:28.330
It was twelve years ago...

14:29.540 --> 14:33.710
The current master was wed to the previous
master's daughter and took on the family name.

14:34.260 --> 14:38.180
Osan-sama was born,
and they were a picture of happiness.

14:39.090 --> 14:43.470
But one day, a band of thieves
called Mishima no Yagyouichimi,

14:43.470 --> 14:47.480
led by a man named Hyakkimaru, came to attack us.

14:56.110 --> 14:56.940
Osan!

15:07.240 --> 15:12.410
Fortunately, Master was saved when he fell
into a cave that was in the middle of the cliff.

15:12.670 --> 15:14.870
Is that what happened?

15:15.330 --> 15:17.290
It was after that incident.

15:17.290 --> 15:21.170
After that incident, the master changed.

15:21.170 --> 15:23.670
It was almost as if he were a totally different person.

15:24.300 --> 15:25.550
And his daughter?

15:25.720 --> 15:28.260
We could not find her... and...

15:31.680 --> 15:33.980
Master, master!

15:36.980 --> 15:38.020
What's happening?

15:38.110 --> 15:41.610
This man is supposedly a fuda-selling
monk who is quite famous in the city.

15:41.940 --> 15:44.900
I was wondering if he would be
able to provide a purification for us...

15:53.290 --> 15:57.790
If he can heal with this,
there's no need for doctors in this world!

16:10.800 --> 16:12.010
It hurts!

16:16.930 --> 16:19.390
Again... again...

16:19.560 --> 16:20.520
S-Save me!

16:21.440 --> 16:25.730
There's only one way to be
saved from the curse of Shio no Chouji.

16:26.570 --> 16:28.690
A-And what is that?

16:28.900 --> 16:32.570
Isn't there some dark deed that you are hiding?

16:33.240 --> 16:36.660
You must tell us everything about it.

16:36.740 --> 16:39.370
E-Even if you say that...

16:39.910 --> 16:42.330
Won't you do it, please?

16:43.080 --> 16:45.870
B-But I don't remember!

16:46.290 --> 16:49.250
Tell us! If you do, you'll be saved!

16:49.960 --> 16:51.500
I don't remember it!

16:51.590 --> 16:52.960
Then you will die.

16:53.510 --> 16:55.920
N-No, s-save me!

17:00.390 --> 17:02.260
Can't you do something?

17:04.060 --> 17:07.770
S-Save me!

17:21.240 --> 17:25.070
Had he honestly confessed
his deeds, he would have been spared.

17:25.080 --> 17:26.580
What a pitiful man.

17:28.000 --> 17:29.700
And what about you?

17:37.880 --> 17:40.960
I'm not really Choujirou!

17:42.090 --> 17:44.720
I'm really Hyakkimaru of the Yagyouichimi!

17:45.010 --> 17:46.840
You're not the master?

17:47.010 --> 17:48.850
You replaced him in that cave, didn't you?

17:48.970 --> 17:50.640
Tihat's impossible!

17:51.560 --> 17:54.980
Choujirou was my younger twin brother.

17:54.980 --> 17:58.600
I had him enter this mansion to work as a spy.

17:58.730 --> 18:00.520
But he betrayed me.

18:00.730 --> 18:03.480
He was diverted by the supposedly "happy" life.

18:03.780 --> 18:06.070
So, I decided to kill everyone...

18:06.900 --> 18:08.280
That's...

18:09.070 --> 18:13.490
That hole... If only I hadn't fallen into that hole!

18:20.420 --> 18:23.000
Do you intend to die here?

18:24.380 --> 18:26.500
I was happy...

18:27.340 --> 18:28.340
I won't die.

18:28.670 --> 18:30.680
I won't die in a place like this!

18:33.760 --> 18:35.510
You ate Hayate!

18:35.890 --> 18:37.930
It was the most delicious thing I had ever tasted.

18:37.930 --> 18:40.850
I couldn't forget that taste,
so I tried various other meats...

18:40.940 --> 18:42.190
Is that why?

18:42.350 --> 18:45.020
But there was nothing that could surpass that taste...

18:45.060 --> 18:46.730
Strange.

18:47.650 --> 18:51.400
The horses' corpses were
discovered at the bottom of the cliff.

18:52.860 --> 18:57.490
Just what did you eat to survive?

19:00.950 --> 19:03.000
Wh-What did I eat?

19:03.040 --> 19:08.290
What you ate were the last
vestiges of your human conscience.

19:20.440 --> 19:21.850
I... I...

19:23.600 --> 19:24.930
Save me!

19:47.910 --> 19:50.620
If you insist on maintaining your
own Way, then you will aggravate people.

19:50.620 --> 19:53.170
But if you stray from your ethics,
you will fall into depravity.

19:53.920 --> 19:56.420
In the end, this world is naught but a dream.

19:56.670 --> 20:02.510
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

20:06.800 --> 20:07.550
Th-This place is...

20:22.570 --> 20:24.740
Save me!

20:42.630 --> 20:44.880
The deed is done.

20:54.890 --> 20:56.010
You!

20:57.680 --> 21:01.480
Sensei, wouldn't you be better
off as an actor, instead of a writer?

21:02.190 --> 21:05.150
Nagamimi-san, that was uncalled for!

21:05.730 --> 21:07.070
You are...

21:07.480 --> 21:11.940
The real Osan-chan lost her
memories after she fell from that cliff,

21:12.650 --> 21:16.910
but now she's at a row house in
Honjou with the abacist, Tokujirou.

21:17.030 --> 21:18.910
How do you know all that?

21:19.290 --> 21:22.700
Listen, just go pick her up tomorrow morning, okay?

21:23.000 --> 21:24.830
Thank you very much!

21:24.920 --> 21:27.670
There's no need to kill all those animals anymore.

21:28.040 --> 21:33.800
But when Master was attacked by
those bandits, I couldn't do anything!

21:34.090 --> 21:38.010
And I killed so that villain could eat...

21:38.260 --> 21:44.010
Forget about that, go get
Osan-chan, and protect this house.

21:50.730 --> 21:53.940
Did you think you were a Kabuki actor or something?

22:02.410 --> 22:03.700
That kid...

22:03.740 --> 22:05.700
...is pretty good, isn't he?

22:05.790 --> 22:09.540
It would be better if he had a sweet tooth.

22:14.760 --> 22:20.850
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:22.200 --> 22:28.290
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:29.270 --> 22:35.040
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:35.080 --> 22:41.710
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:43.080 --> 22:49.020
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:49.060 --> 22:55.720
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:56.560 --> 23:06.030
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:07.340 --> 23:10.540
Draw near

23:10.810 --> 23:17.810
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:17.850 --> 23:23.790
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:25.960 --> 23:31.230
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:31.270 --> 23:39.900
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:51.190 --> 23:56.650
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:57.320 --> 23:59.320
There is a troop of puppeteers, Shibaemon.

23:59.860 --> 24:02.200
[Note: A tanuki is a Japanese raccoon.]

23:59.860 --> 24:02.200
There is a tanuki that takes human shape.

24:02.740 --> 24:05.580
[Note: Mamono refers to diabolic youkai,
ayakashi is another synonym for youkai.]

24:02.740 --> 24:05.580
Is it a murderous mamono, or an ayakashi?

24:06.040 --> 24:10.080
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:10.620 --> 24:12.130
Shibaemon Tanuki

24:13.380 --> 24:15.540
The deed is done.
